<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">27 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 27 March, from 1329 to 1980.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/pope-john-xxii" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pope-john-xxii.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1329">1329 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">697 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Pope John XXII condemns writings of Meister Eckhart as heretical</h2><p class="tih-event-desc"><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-john-xxii">Pope John XXII</a> condemned many writings of Meister Eckhart as heretical in the papal bull In Agro Dominico. Eckhart was a German priest, theologian, philosopher and mystic of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dominican-order">Dominican Order</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pope-john-xxii">Pope John XXII</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1513">1513 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">513 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Juan Ponce de León sights Florida</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Sailing north from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a>, Ponce de León sighted the coast he named La <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a>, as it was the Easter season. He landed days later, beginning Spanish claims to the region.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puerto-rico">Puerto Rico</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1625">1625 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">401 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Charles I becomes king on the death of James I</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">James I died at Theobalds and his son succeeded him. Charles's clashes with Parliament over money and religion led to civil war and his execution in 1649.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1782">1782 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">244 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Marquess of Rockingham forms his second British ministry</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Charles Watson-Wentworth, 2nd Marquess of Rockingham, took office in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Great Britain</a> at the head of a ministry that began negotiations to end the American War of Independence. His second premiership lasted four months.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-great-britain">Kingdom of Great Britain</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1794">1794 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">232 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Congress passes the Naval Act, founding the US Navy</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Prompted by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/barbary-coast">Barbary</a> corsairs seizing American ships, Congress authorised six frigates. Among them was USS Constitution, still in commission today.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1871">1871 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">155 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Scotland and England play the first rugby international</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At Raeburn Place in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/edinburgh">Edinburgh</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a> beat <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a> by a goal and a try to a try before about 4,000 spectators. It was the first international rugby match.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scotland">Scotland</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1977">1977 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">49 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Two jumbo jets collide at Tenerife</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A KLM 747 began its take-off in fog and struck a Pan Am 747 on the runway at Los Rodeos airport, killing 583 people. It remains the deadliest accident in aviation history.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1980">1980 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">46 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Mount St Helens erupts for the first time in 123 years</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">A steam explosion blasted a crater in the summit of the Washington volcano after a week of earthquakes. On 18 May a massive eruption tore away its north face and killed 57 people.</p></div></li></ol>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-born"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-born">Born on 27 March <span class="n">4</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/albert-iii-duke-of-bavaria"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/albert-iii-duke-of-bavaria.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Albert III, Duke of Bavaria</span><span class="tp">1401–1460</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-ii-rakoczi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-ii-rakoczi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francis II Rákóczi</span><span class="tp">1676–1735</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/georges-eugene-haussmann"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/georges-eugene-haussmann.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Georges-Eugène Haussmann</span><span class="tp">1809–1891</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/sandor-garbai"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/sandor-garbai.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Sándor Garbai</span><span class="tp">1879–1947</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<section class="day-ppl" aria-labelledby="day-died"><h2 class="ref-sec-title" id="day-died">Died on 27 March <span class="n">9</span></h2><ul class="enc-seealso"><li><a href="/encyclopedia/hermann-billung"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/hermann-billung.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Hermann Billung</span><span class="tp">d. 973</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/pope-gregory-xi"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/pope-gregory-xi.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Pope Gregory XI</span><span class="tp">c. 1329–1378</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/vasily-ii-of-moscow"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/vasily-ii-of-moscow.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Vasily II of Moscow</span><span class="tp">1415–1462</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/mary-of-burgundy"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/mary-of-burgundy.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Mary of Burgundy</span><span class="tp">1457–1482</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/james-vi-and-i"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/james-vi-and-i.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">James VI and I</span><span class="tp">1566–1625</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/giovanni-battista-tiepolo"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/giovanni-battista-tiepolo.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Giovanni Battista Tiepolo</span><span class="tp">1696–1770</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/francis-william-reitz"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/francis-william-reitz.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Francis William Reitz</span><span class="tp">1844–1934</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/michael-joseph-savage"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/michael-joseph-savage.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Michael Joseph Savage</span><span class="tp">1872–1940</span></span></a></li><li><a href="/encyclopedia/yuri-gagarin"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/thumbs/yuri-gagarin.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="44" height="44"><span><span class="nm">Yuri Gagarin</span><span class="tp">1934–1968</span></span></a></li></ul></section>
<p class="day-ppl-note">Dates as the sources give them: in the Julian calendar before 1582, and in some countries for longer (Britain until 1752, Russia until 1918). Only people whose day of birth or death the records agree on are listed.</p>
